132
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:13,260
For most of American history, retail business had been conducted on the local level.

133
00:08:14,820 --> 00:08:19,560
Many mom-and-pop stores were small family affairs that offered a limited line of products.

134
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:26,900
But with the rise of the family automobile in the 1950s, America expanded beyond the cities.

135
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:31,380
Suburbs and superhighways were quickly transforming the way we lived.

136
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:37,720
And as America grew, so did the need for stores that could keep up with the increase in demand.

137
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:43,940
The term megastore leaves the impression that these large-scale commercial retailers were always big, and they weren't.

138
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:47,960
Megastores as we know them today have only been around for the last 50 years or so,

139
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:53,700
