155
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:23,680
Everything else is loaded onto a system of conveyor belts, nearly two and a half miles long.

156
00:10:24,680 --> 00:10:29,600
As soon as each product hits the conveyor belt, a barcode tracking label is attached to it.

157
00:10:29,601 --> 00:10:36,240
After that label is applied, a complex reader will read the barcode information, and that

158
00:10:36,241 --> 00:10:40,860
barcode tells the system which store it should be sent to.

159
00:10:40,861 --> 00:10:45,340
Using the information relayed by the barcode, a sorter routes each product down a divert

160
00:10:45,341 --> 00:10:50,920
